//- The language v0.8 in one diagram (FORMAT §3.2.3–§3.2.9): lines, Markdown, tables, category,
//- states, legend, plain text, docking.
diagram(dir="right")
  title Shop — AWS production platform
    | Account 123456789012 · eu-west-3 (Paris) · 106 resources
    |.pill prod

  card#users.ext Customers
    | shop / www → CDN
    to(alb).user HTTPS
  zone#vpc.vpc(tag="module.network") VPC 10.20.0.0/16
    | 3 availability zones · flow logs to CloudWatch
    card#alb.app(label="Load balancer (ALB)" tag="module.app") shop-prod
      | :443 HTTPS (**TLS 1.3**)
      to(lambda).user :8080
    card#lambda.fn.warn(label="Lambda (in VPC)" tag="module.functions") order_events
      | `python3.12` · 256 MB
      |.warn db SG has no rule for the lambda SG
      to(db).data 5432
    card#db.data(label="RDS PostgreSQL 16.4" tag="module.data") shop-prod-orders
      | Multi-AZ · ==14-day backups==

  card#flows.legend(at="ne") Flows
    |.user user request
    |.data data access

  zone#sec(at="s") Security & identity
    card#kms(label="KMS key") alias/shop-prod-data
      | encrypts RDS, SQS, S3
    card#sg(label="Security groups") Ingress
      | Group  | Inbound                    | Attached to   |
      |--------|----------------------------|---------------|
      | alb    | 443, 80 from ==0.0.0.0/0== | load balancer |
      | api    | 8080 from alb              | ECS api tasks |
      | ^^     | 9090 from monitoring       | ECS api tasks |
      | worker | no inbound rule           ||
      |.error lambda | none                 | order_events  |
  zone#ops(at="s") Monitoring & operations
    card#alarms(label="CloudWatch alarms") 5-min average
      | db_cpu > 80 % · ==.ok OK==
      to(sns)
    card#sns(label="SNS topic") shop-prod-alerts
      | email: on-call

  card.text.wide(at="s")
    |.warn = finding worth reviewing
    | Omitted for clarity: route tables (12), IAM policy attachments.
